WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Hey, welcome to Tesla Short's Time Daily episode 426.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.460
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.940
Today is April 4th, 2026.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.140
Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.820
Let's start with a pretty remarkable win on the sales front.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.020
Tesla has moved ahead of BYD and the global electric vehicle

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.280
market according to the latest quarterly figures.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.380
This shift happened even though the broader EV market

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.940
is showing some signs of cooling off in certain regions,

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.380
which makes the result feel a bit more earned.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.200
For Tesla's business, this outcome reinforces

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.860
its position as the volume leader in electric vehicles,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.260
something the company has fought hard to maintain

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.060
through multiple product cycles and economic ups and downs.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.240
It is worth noting that holding on to that top spot

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.460
requires consistent execution across multiple continents,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.900
from strong performance in North America

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.060
to recovering momentum in China and selective growth elsewhere.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.200
From a competitive landscape perspective,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.160
this puts pressure on other manufacturers

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.860
who had been closing the gap over the past couple of years,

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.860
especially as some traditional automakers ramp up

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.160
their own EV offerings.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.060
I find it encouraging that Tesla achieve this

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.360
without relying on a single dominant market,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.640
showing the strength of its global footprint

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.460
and the appeal of its product lineup

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.540
even when overall demand is uneven.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.060
That top line success gives us a good jumping off point

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.140
to look at what's happening inside the factories

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.840
because sales numbers only tell part of the story.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.820
Tesla's workforce at Giga, Texas,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.760
is shrank by nearly 5,000 workers last year.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.060
That represents about a 22% reduction

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.520
at the company's largest United States facility,

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.660
which is a pretty substantial change

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.940
when you think about the scale of operations there.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.240
The drop was identified through public records reviewed

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.320
by the Austin American Statesman,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.220
giving us a clearer picture than the usual vague corporate updates.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.100
It reflects deliberate streamlining efforts

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.460
as the company looks to improve manufacturing efficiency

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.520
after years of rapid hiring during the initial ramp up

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.080
of the Cybertruck and other lines.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.700
In business terms, this kind of adjustment

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.120
can help control costs while maintaining

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.740
or even increasing output,

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.780
which is critical when margins are under pressure

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.860
from pricing actions and incentives.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.180
Still workforce changes at this scale

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.740
always raise questions about how the remaining team

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.000
will absorb the workload,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.880
whether there's enough institutional knowledge left

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.460
and how morale holds up during the transition.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.960
These moves are never easy,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.280
but they often signal a company trying to shift

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.800
from growth at all costs

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.660
to something more sustainable and productive.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.160
Efficiency moves at home or one thing,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.740
but demand stimulation and key international markets

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.340
is equally important right now.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.580
Tesla is offering free supercharging to customers in China

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.580
and Japan when they trade in a vehicle

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.760
or take advantage of limited time promotions.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.620
The incentives are aimed at boosting sales

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.000
and loyalty and two important Asian markets

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.980
where competition has been intensifying

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.860
and where brand loyalty can make a real difference over time.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.460
Other regions are experiencing softer demand,

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.620
making these targeted offers particularly strategic

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.860
rather than a blanket global discount

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.640
that would hurt margins everywhere.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.040
Free supercharging has long been one

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.780
of Tesla's most effective customer retention tools,

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.760
creating a sense of ongoing value

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.460
that goes beyond the initial purchase

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.000
and encourages owners to stay within the ecosystem.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.000
By tying it to trade-ins,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.860
the company can accelerate fleet renewal

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.400
while giving buyers immediate, tangible value

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.780
that feels more meaningful than a simple price cut.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.040
Those incentives tie directly into the mixed picture

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.700
we are seeing on inventory in Europe

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.660
where the story is more complicated

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.660
than the global sales win might suggest.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.360
Tesla beat BYD in first quarter electric vehicle sales

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.460
but the victory comes with rising inventory

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.420
and a noticeable sales slump in Europe.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.180
High inventory levels can pressure pricing in margins

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.460
if not managed carefully,

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.480
especially when storage and financing costs

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.460
start to add up across multiple continents.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.480
The company is responding with the free supercharging offers

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.220
we just discussed plus continued software improvements

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.360
that make existing vehicles more appealing to hesitant buyers.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.220
According to reports,

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:02.240
the European slowdown reflects broader market conditions

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.900
rather than Tesla's specific issues alone

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.700
with high interest rates and economic uncertainty

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.640
affecting the whole industry in that region.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.740
Balancing production with real-time demand

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.300
remains one of the more difficult

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.340
operational challenges Tesla faces,

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.200
particularly as factories have been optimized for higher volumes.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.260
It is a reminder that even strong quarterly rankings

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.780
do not eliminate the need for constant adjustment

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.960
in both production and marketing strategies.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.680
While sales and inventory dominate the headlines,

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.940
a wild safety story out of Israel

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.800
is getting a lot of attention and deserves its own moment.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.720
A Tesla vehicle in Israel absorbed a direct strike

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.320
from Iranian missile debris,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.920
remarkably the glass roof remained intact

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.800
despite the impact, which is the kind of real-world test

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.060
no crash lab could ever fully replicate.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.160
This incident highlights the structural resilience built

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:54.580
into Tesla's design under unexpected real-world stress,

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.340
showing how the combination of materials

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.640
and engineering choices can perform when it matters most.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.900
It goes beyond typical crash test scenarios

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.700
and speaks to the overall toughness

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.120
of the vehicle architecture,

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.360
including the way the roof integrates

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.800
with the rest of the body structure.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.920
Stories like this tend to boost customer confidence

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.520
in ways that marketing materials rarely achieve

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.020
because they feel authentic and unscripted.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.580
The fact that the car protected its occupants

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:24.360
in such an extreme situation is genuinely impressive

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.100
and serves as a powerful,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.860
if unintended advertisement for build quality.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.580
From one impressive real-world example to another,

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.200
it's worth looking at how Teslas

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.800
are performing in the used market,

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.740
which tells us a lot about long-term ownership value.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.160
Four Tesla models rank among the 20 fastest-selling

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.600
used vehicles according to current market data.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.000
This strong resale demand persists,

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.440
even as new vehicle inventories have been rising,

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.780
which is interesting because it shows buyers

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.000
still see Tesla as a desirable choice,

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.040
even in a softer new car environment.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.640
It represents good news for existing owners

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.660
through better retained value over time,

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.300
something that can significantly lower the true cost

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.540
of ownership when you factor in depreciation.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.340
A healthy secondary market also makes it easier

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.260
for new buyers to enter the ecosystem,

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.500
whether through certified pre-owned programs

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.920
or private sales,

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.120
because they know the cars hold their worth reasonably well.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:20.160
In practical terms, this means lower effective ownership costs

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.460
for people who choose Tesla compared to some other EVs

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.900
that depreciate more sharply.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.860
Strong-used market performance makes the absence

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.660
of certain models in certain countries

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.820
even more noticeable,

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.240
especially when customer demand seems clear.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.500
A six-seat Tesla SUV priced at $48,500

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.820
is currently sold in eight countries.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.580
However, it remains unavailable in the United States market,

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.360
which continues to puzzle a lot of potential buyers here.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.980
Many American buyers have specifically asked

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.580
for this type of family vehicle,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.720
particularly those with larger households

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.000
who want the versatility of three rows

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.200
without stepping up to something much more expensive.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.200
The situation raises legitimate questions

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.960
about Tesla's regional product allocation decisions

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.540
and whether they're prioritizing certain markets

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.940
based on volume projections or regulatory considerations.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.520
Offering the six-seater in more markets

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.120
could address a clear segment of customer demand

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.060
that currently feels underserved.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.020
It highlights the occasional disconnect between what buyers are requesting

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.720
and what actually reaches showrooms,

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.560
even when the product already exists elsewhere.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.400
On the retail side,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.400
Tesla is clearly pushing harder into one key market

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.000
that could use more physical presence.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.920
Tesla is growing its retail footprint in Japan

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.000
with plans for more than 60 stores.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.100
The expansion aims to improve both sales presence

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.420
and service capability across the country,

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.560
addressing a long-standing complaint

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.140
about limited access to test drives and maintenance.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:50.180
The stated goal is to become the leading imported brand in that market,

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.080
which would be a significant achievement

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.600
given how loyal Japanese buyers tend to be

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.980
to domestic manufacturers.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.380
Japan has historically been a challenging environment

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.800
for foreign automakers due to tight competition,

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:03.540
different consumer preferences,

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.040
and a preference for smaller, efficient vehicles.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.640
Success here could open a significant new avenue for growth

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.780
if Tesla executes well and manages

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.240
to adapt its offerings and messaging appropriately.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.820
It represents a serious long-term bet

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.540
on the Asian market beyond China,

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.980
showing the company is thinking strategically about diversification.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.260
While Japan gets more physical stores,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.220
software progress continues for customers in Europe

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.620
who have been waiting patiently for new features.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.220
The latest software update labeled 2026.8.6

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.860
is being pushed to vehicles.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:40.120
Release notes include hints that full-self-driving version 14

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.440
could soon arrive in Europe,

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.660
which many owners have been anticipating for quite some time.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.840
This signals expanded capabilities

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.160
and regional readiness outside North America,

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.980
potentially unlocking features

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.260
that have been available in other markets for months.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:54.840
For many European owners,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.560
this represents an important step

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.300
after waiting through multiple regulatory hurdles

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.540
and delayed rollouts.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.960
The update demonstrates Tesla's continued focus

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:06.440
on iterative software development rather than big-bang annual releases,

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.820
which has become their signature approach.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.480
Regulatory approval processes in Europe

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.720
tend to move deliberately,

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.160
so this progress matters

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.340
and could set the stage for wider adoption

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.320
if the initial data looks solid.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.120
That software momentum is also showing up

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.240
in community conversations about unsupervised driving

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.260
where owners are sharing more practical experiences.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.940
A recent podcast discussion highlighted

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.660
real-world unsupervised,

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.020
full-self-driving experiences in Austin.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.080
The conversation featured insights

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.780
into how the technology performs

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.440
during day-to-day operation,

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.480
including both the impressive moments

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.040
and the occasional limitations.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.380
It is generating fresh owner discussions

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.240
about when similar capabilities might expand further

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.480
and what regulatory changes would be needed.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.520
Hearing from people actually using the system

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.300
provides a grounded perspective

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.740
that cuts through some of the more breathless coverage out there.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.520
These kinds of real-world reports help separate hype

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.840
from actual capability

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.680
and give Tesla valuable feedback

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.060
for the next iterations.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.240
Community feedback like this often influences

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.620
how quickly Tesla iterates on the software,

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.320
creating a loop between developers and users

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.560
that feels pretty unique in the auto industry.

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.040
On the competitive front,

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.180
Lucid reported lower than expected first-quarter deliveries,

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:26.020
a supplier disruption paused sales of its gravity model

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.040
for nearly a month,

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.200
which shows how fragile supply chains can still be

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.940
even for well-capitalized players.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.720
The situation highlights ongoing challenges

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.980
and scaling luxury electric vehicle production,

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:38.180
particularly when you're trying

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.920
to maintain high-quality standards

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:41.200
and unique design elements.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:45.180
For Tesla, it serves as a useful reminder of execution risks

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:47.340
that even well-funded competitors face,

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.620
suggesting that consistent delivery numbers

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.780
are harder than they look.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.700
Different companies encounter different bottlenecks

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.180
at various stages of growth,

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.740
whether it's suppliers, regulatory approvals,

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.220
or internal ramp-up issues.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:03.020
It puts Tesla's own scaling efforts in some perspective,

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.140
especially when you consider how many vehicles

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.000
they're moving despite their own challenges.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.620
Toyota's updated electric crossover

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.420
posted strong sales growth

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.480
in the United States during the first quarter.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.420
The improvement suggests traditional automakers

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.040
are making measurable progress

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.680
in the battery electric segment

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.700
after years of more cautious approaches.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.580
This adds competitive pressure on Tesla,

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.400
particularly in the crossover market,

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.540
which has become a key battleground

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:32.000
as families look for practical EV's legacy manufacturers

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.160
bring decades of customer relationships

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.560
and distribution networks

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.300
that Tesla still has to build in many areas.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.220
Tesla will need to keep innovating

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.940
to maintain its edge as more options

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.720
reach the market

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.980
and as brand loyalty for established names

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:45.800
comes into play.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.000
It is healthy for the entire electric vehicle industry

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.400
when multiple players advance

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.420
because it helps normalize the technology

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.060
and builds overall infrastructure and acceptance.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.880
Production of both the Model S and Model X

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:58.920
has now wrapped up.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:02.040
Tesla is shifting focus toward newer platforms,

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.240
including upcoming Robotaxi

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.160
and next-generation vehicles

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.600
that promise to be more efficient and scalable.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.740
The move has sparked conversation

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.600
among buyers who preferred those larger sedans

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.560
and SUV's, some of whom feel

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.240
like they're losing beloved models

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:18.820
that helped define the brand.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.160
It marks a clear strategic bet

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.120
on the future architecture of the company,

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.040
moving away from the older platform

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.180
that has been in production for over a decade.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.820
Flagship models played an important role

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:31.800
in establishing the brand early on

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.360
and proving that electric cars

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.140
could be desirable and high performance.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.520
Their discontinuation feels significant

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.140
even if it aligns with long-term product planning

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:41.380
and resource allocation

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:43.180
toward higher volume future products.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.000
National average gas prices

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.340
crossing the $4 mark

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:48.380
have revived interest in electric vehicles.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.860
This external factor is helping lift

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.960
Tesla's recent sales to some degree,

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.480
particularly among buyers

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.880
who were on the fence about total cost of ownership.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.660
It shows how energy prices

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:01.280
continue to influence electric vehicle adoption

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.800
years into the transition,

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.840
acting as a recurring catalyst

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.380
when fuel costs spike.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.560
Higher fuel costs provide a timely tailwind

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.840
as the company manages inventory levels

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.160
and tries to clear lots.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.340
Consumer behavior often responds

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.820
to immediate economic signals at the pump

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:21.040
rather than long-term environmental considerations alone.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.740
Still, sustainable growth will need

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.380
to rely on more than temporary price fluctuations,

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.100
which is why the software

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.860
and product roadmap remain so critical.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.740
Reports indicate Tesla has accumulated

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:36.020
a notable number of unsolved vehicles.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.620
This inventory buildup persists

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:40.640
even as buyer interest improves

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.120
with higher gas prices,

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.420
creating a bit of a timing mismatch.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.000
The mismatch between production output

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.700
and immediate demand requires careful balancing

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.340
to avoid deep discounting

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.880
that could damage brand perception.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.860
Managing inventory effectively remains

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.940
one of the trickier aspects of the business,

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.140
especially when factories are tuned

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.060
for high throughput.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.020
Tesla will likely use a combination

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.740
of incentives and product updates

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:05.820
to move these vehicles

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.580
without resorting to heavy price cuts

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.360
across the board.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.680
It is an area worth watching closely

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:11.560
in the coming quarters

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.480
because it directly impacts profitability

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:15.240
and how the market perceives demand.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.420
Taking a step back from the headlines,

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:19.200
it is useful to consider

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.140
the underlying economics of unsupervised autonomy.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.220
Training and running the neural networks

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.460
for self-driving requires enormous amounts

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:28.600
of electricity and specialized silicon

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.540
costs that aren't always obvious

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.540
when you focus only on the vehicle side.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.000
The marginal cost per mile needs

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.980
to eventually drop below the cost

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:39.180
of a human driver for the business case

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:41.140
to close, which is a high bar

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:42.340
when you factor in everything.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.440
Each inference cycle for vision-based planning

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.920
uses a transformer model

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.680
that is particularly compute-heavy,

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.180
demanding both power

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.800
and careful thermal management.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:54.100
Real-world operation at scale

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.600
could require thousands of watts

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.660
during active driving,

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:57.880
making fleet utilization

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.860
and energy sourcing key variables.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.200
The ratio of useful miles driven

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.360
versus idle time becomes the decisive

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:05.680
variable in profitability,

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.860
which is why Tesla talks so much

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.280
about high utilization robot taxi networks.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.420
Tesla has consistently solved

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:13.320
similar problems

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.600
through vertical integration

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:15.900
of hardware and software,

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.080
giving them an advantage over companies

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.400
that rely on multiple outside suppliers.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.440
By owning the entire stack

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.960
from Dojo Supercomputers

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.780
to vehicle hardware and fleet data,

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.860
they can optimize both silicon

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.660
and energy systems together

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.500
in ways that would be difficult for others.

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:33.220
If the total energy

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.720
and compute cost per mile

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:35.840
can be driven low enough

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.940
while maintaining high-fleet utilization,

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.640
then unsupervised autonomy

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:41.340
becomes economically superior

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.740
to traditional ride-hailing.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.680
Until that threshold is reached,

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.820
the physics and economics keep it firmly

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:47.980
in the development column,

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.200
which is why patience

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.580
remains important even as the demos look impressive.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.680
Before we go keep an eye on how

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.620
the European software rollout progresses

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.060
and whether the Japan's

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.700
store expansion gains momentum

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.660
in the weeks ahead.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.480
Those two areas could tell us a lot

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.220
about Tesla's international trajectory

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.180
in the coming months.

